# `manifest.json` is read from disk and hashed byte-exactly against
# MANIFEST_SHA256 (crates/wallet-core/src/channelpay_interop.rs), so its bytes
# have to be the same on every machine. It is the only i/lf file here; the ten
# .bin vectors beside it are already binary to git and are never rewritten.
#
# Without this, a Windows clone with core.autocrlf=true materialises it CRLF,
# the digest moves, and the test fails with "Official ChannelPay fixture
# manifest digest mismatch" - which reads as fixture tampering rather than as
# line endings. No CI job runs it today; a Windows developer's first fresh
# clone does.
#
# `text eol=lf` and not `text=auto`: text=auto still defers to core.autocrlf
# and would leave it CRLF on Windows, fixing nothing.
manifest.json text eol=lf
*.bin -text
